{
  "_comment": "What the agent's setup proposal tool takes, shared by both plugins. `items`: each item as the agent sent it, and either what is stored in the proposals file (`stored`) or the error the agent gets back for it (`error`). A grant must be one `grant <kind> <pattern> --persistent [--allows ...] [--expires ...]` would accept, a binding one `bind add` would add that could ever apply, and either one the setup screen can show; session grants, settings and attended platforms are refused, and a destination may use a wildcard only as `*.` and one registrable domain. `calls`: the tool's whole answer to a call's arguments (with {setup} replaced by /sentrook setup on Hermes and /sentrook-setup on OpenClaw) and how many items it stores; items sent as JSON text read as the list it holds. `store`: the proposals file before and after a proposal is stored at `now` from `session_ref`, with ids drawn in the order `ids` gives: at most three open, a new one replacing the oldest, expired ones dropped. `unchecked_warning`: the line the setup screen shows on each item of a proposal made while the chat had read content no scan had seen yet.",
  "refusal": "Setup needs the owner in a direct chat.",
